From 71720520b2f7d9ef73bb54875de22be0295f0f51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:46:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Move cockpit pins clear of MSRC's, add bootscreen-delay
 config

Ralph confirmed this chip will eventually also run real MSRC
telemetry (vario/GPS/ESC/...), so the cockpit's display/servo/IMU
pins need to live somewhere that never collides with constants.h's
MSRC pins, not just document the overlap.

This board is the RP2350B variant (48 GPIOs), and the pico-sdk ships
its exact definition as "waveshare_core2350b" - the project was
building against the generic 30-GPIO "pico2" (RP2350A) board instead,
which is why there wasn't room before. Switching to the correct board
(see README.md for the cmake command) exposes GPIO32-47, so every
cockpit pin now sits at 32 or above, clear of MSRC's 0-15/26-29 and
of the onboard LED/WS2812 pins (39/16). Verified by a full clean
build against -DPICO_BOARD=waveshare_core2350b.

Also in cockpit_pins.h: COCKPIT_BOOTSCREEN_MS, replacing a hardcoded
4000 in cockpit_task.c, and a new cockpit/README.md collecting the
build command, the pin file, and how to swap map_bitmap.h - one page
to come back to instead of re-deriving it after a break.

Not fixed here, flagged in both files: board/project/sensor/
{voltage,current,ntc,airspeed}.c hardcode "+ 26" to get a GPIO from
an ADC channel, which only matches the 30-GPIO board's ADC pins
(26-29) - on this corrected board those are GPIO40-47 instead. Only
matters if one of those four sensors is enabled on this chip; fix
belongs on rp2350-port first per our branch split.

